      "dimension_source": "rubric",
      "dimension_name": "Sequencing logic",
      "llm_score": 2,
      "corrected_score": 2,
      "comment": "I checked the order of all 13 plan items and their fallback relationships. The sequence is generally logical, starting with the death certificate as direct parentage evidence, followed by census searches and supporting family records. Prioritizing the 1880 census before 1870 is defensible because it includes the relationship-to-head column. However, the Orphans' Court item (pli_014) is described as a fallback to the probate item (pli_013), but its fallback_for field is null. The formal fallback link should be added to preserve that relationship."
    },
